<title>UK: UB says wins &quot;passing off&quot; action.</title>
<headline>UB says wins &quot;passing off&quot; action.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Biscuits(Holdings) Plc (UB) said on Tuesday that the High Court has upheld its claim against supermarket chain ASDA Group Plc Plc that it was guilty of &quot;passing off&quot; and its Puffin biscuit presentation was &quot;deceptively similar&quot; to UB's Penguin.</p>
<p>ASDA has been required to remove their product from the shelves within 35 days, said UB in a statement. Earlier ASDA claimed victory saying the High Court had ruled it could continue to call its biscuits Puffins, allbeit with minor changes to the packaging. But UB cast doubt on this claim.</p>
<p>&quot;When ASDA requested the court to clarify that it could use the Puffin name in future Justice Walker declined to do so,&quot; said UB.</p>
<p>- London newsroom +44 171 542 6437</p>
